# video_slotmgr_invariants.sby — VIDEO.SLOTMGR ownership invariants
# (reports/DEBUG.FRAMEBLIT_Integration_Corrections.md section 9).
#
#   at most one slot is DISPLAYED, and the bookkeeping agrees with the states
#   a lease grant implies the slot was FREE the instant before
#   a grant moves that slot's generation by exactly one, and nothing else does
#   a live lease always points at a slot that is WRITING
#   a publication moves WRITING -> READY only on a MATCHING generation
#   a release moves WRITING -> FREE only on a MATCHING generation
#   a STALE event changes no state, and is counted
#   slot_ready means READY, exactly
#
# Two of the eight properties the review lists -- never WRITING and DISPLAYED at
# once, never READY and WRITING at once -- are true by the two-bit encoding and
# are named in the RTL rather than asserted, because asserting them would prove
# a property of `logic [1:0]` and not of this design.
#
# The DUT is driven with EVERY input free: arbitrary lease requests, arbitrary
# publications and releases carrying arbitrary generations, and arbitrary swaps.
# That is the adversarial model the invariants need -- can any sequence of
# events, however malformed, get two slots on screen at once or slip a stale
# publication past the generation check?
#
# SCOPE-TOTAL: the state space is two slots x four states x one outstanding
# lease, and the depth below covers the complete FREE -> WRITING -> READY ->
# DISPLAYED -> FREE cycle for both slots plus a stale re-grant. The generation
# counter is 16 bits and is NOT explored exhaustively -- the properties above
# constrain it by equality and increment-by-one rather than by value, so no
# bound on its magnitude is being claimed.
#
# TWO TASKS, both required (ledger rule V16):
#   bmc   — the invariants hold to the depth below.
#   cover — every antecedent is REACHABLE. All eight assertions are
#           implications; a model that can never grant, publish, swap or go
#           stale satisfies them all while proving nothing.
#
# Run via `ctest -L formal` or by hand with cwd = tests/formal:
#   sby -f --prefix <workdir> video_slotmgr_invariants.sby

[tasks]
bmc
cover

[options]
bmc:   mode bmc
bmc:   depth 24
cover: mode cover
cover: depth 24
expect pass

[engines]
btor btormc

[script]
read_slang --top zhao_video_slotmgr -DFORMAL zhao_video_slotmgr.sv
prep -top zhao_video_slotmgr

[files]
../../fpga/rtl/video/zhao_video_slotmgr.sv
